Given the following text and a relational triplet extracted from it:

Text: Get emergency medical help if you have signs of an allergic reaction to levothyroxine: hives, difficult breathing, swelling of your face, lips, tongue, or throat. Allergic reactions are usually caused by the inactive ingredients in a product rather than by levothyroxine itself, so your doctor may suggest trying a different brand or form.
Levothyroxine may cause serious side effects. Call your doctor at once if you have:
- sudden pain or trouble moving your hip, wrist, or back;
- fast or irregular heartbeats, or a pounding heartbeat;
- chest pain, pain spreading to your jaw or shoulder;
- wheezing or shortness of breath;
- swelling in your legs or ankles, or new or worsening breathlessness when lying down;
- fever, swollen glands, itching, joint pain, or not feeling well;
- nausea, vomiting, or diarrhea;
- confusion or feeling disoriented;
- a seizure; or
- high blood sugar - increased thirst, increased urination, dry mouth, fruity breath odor.
Common levothyroxine side effects may include:
- fever, hot flashes, increased sweating, feeling too hot;
- tiredness;
Triplet: ["levothyroxine", "may cause", "sudden pain or trouble moving hip"]

The relation 'may cause' in the triplet is defined as 'The subject drug is associated with the occurrence of the condition or symptom specified by the object entity.' In this context, is there any relation appropriate to replace it? Please answer by providing only the letter of your choice.

Choices:
A. 'has side effect': The subject drug may cause the adverse effect or symptom specified by the object entity.
B. 'treats': The subject drug is used to treat or manage the disease or medical condition specified by the object entity.
C. 'has overdose symptom': An overdose of the subject drug may cause the symptom specified by the object entity.
D. 'interacts with': The subject drug has a drug interaction with the drug or substance specified by the object entity that may change effects or cause harm.
E. 'increases risk of': Taking the subject drug may raise the patient's likelihood of experiencing the condition or event specified by the object entity.
F. None of the above.

Answer:
